IMPORT `spc-nouns`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, Schedule 3 (Enactments repealed).
--
-- Schedule 3 is a table of repeals in three other Acts, the repealing provision that
-- section 21 points at. As rendered in the deposited text the rows repeal single
-- connecting words ("and", "or") and one subsection (section 148(4) of the
-- Contributions and Benefits Act). A repeal changes the text of another Act; it
-- creates no relation between a claimant and anyone and asks no question of one.
-- The deposited text renders the table as rows of the form
-- `| Short title and chapter | Extent of repeal |`. Nothing is encoded, so the file
-- holds only the quotation and this reason.

§ `Schedule 3 -- Enactments repealed`

-- src:671 | Schedule 3 — Enactments repealed
-- src:672 | | Short title and chapter | Extent of repeal |
-- src:673 | | Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (c. 4) | In section 124(1), the word “and” immediately preceding paragraph (f).Section 148(4). |
-- src:674 | | Social Security Act 1998 (c. 14) | In section 2(2), the word “or” immediately preceding paragraph (h).In section 11(3), in the definition of “current legislation”, the word “and” in the second place where it occurs.In section 28(3), the word “or” immediately preceding paragraph (e).In paragraph 6(b) of Schedule 2, the word “or” immediately preceding sub-paragraph (ii). |
-- src:675 | | Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (c. 11) | In section 10(3), the word “or” immediately preceding paragraph (b). |
-- (not encoded: Schedule 3 lists words repealed in the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, the Social Security Act 1998 and the Social Security Fraud Act 2001; it asks nothing of a claimant)
